# Always Use Bun

This project uses Bun as the JavaScript runtime and toolkit.

## Key Documentation References
@https://bun.sh/docs
@https://bun.sh/guides/read-file
@https://bun.sh/guides/write-file
@https://bun.sh/blog/bun-macros
@https://bun.sh/docs/bundler
@https://bun.sh/docs/bundler/html

## Core Features

### Runtime
- Fast JavaScript/TypeScript runtime (drop-in Node.js replacement)
- Written in Zig and powered by JavaScriptCore for improved performance
- Native TypeScript and JSX support without configuration
- Significantly faster startup times and lower memory usage

### Package Management
- Node.js-compatible package manager
- Fast installation with `bun install <pkg>`
- Automatically generates lockfiles
- Compatible with existing Node.js projects

### Bundler
- Fast JavaScript/TypeScript bundler with `bun build`
- Support for bundling multiple entrypoints
- CSS bundling with `@import` support and asset handling
- Macros for bundle-time code execution
- HTML bundling

### Testing
- Built-in test runner with `bun test`
- Jest-compatible API
- Fast execution

### File System
- High-performance file system APIs
- Simple read/write APIs:
  - `Bun.file(path).text()` - Read as string
  - `Bun.file(path).json()` - Read as JSON
  - `Bun.write(path, content)` - Write files
- File watching capabilities

### HTTP & WebSockets
- Native HTTP server implementation
- WebSocket server support
- Fast request handling

### Development Workflow
- Script running with `bun run`
- Package execution with `bunx`
- Project templates

## Common Commands
```bash
# Run a script directly
bun run index.tsx

# Run a script defined in package.json
bun run start

# Install dependencies
bun install

# Add a specific package
bun add react

# Bundle a project
bun build ./index.tsx --outdir ./out

# Run tests
bun test

# Execute a package
bunx cowsay 'Hello, world!'
```

## Examples

### Embed Git Commit Hash (Bun Macros)
```typescript
// getGitCommitHash.ts
export function getGitCommitHash() {
  const {stdout} = Bun.spawnSync({
    cmd: ["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"],
    stdout: "pipe",
  });
  return stdout.toString();
}

// in-the-browser.ts
import { getGitCommitHash } from './getGitCommitHash.ts' with { type: 'macro' };
console.log(`The current Git commit hash is ${getGitCommitHash()}`);
```

### Simple React App Bundling
```typescript
// Build a React app
await Bun.build({
  entrypoints: ['./index.tsx'],
  outdir: './out',
})

// Or via CLI
// bun build ./index.tsx --outdir ./out
```

### File Operations
```typescript
// Read a file
const text = await Bun.file("path/to/file.txt").text();
const json = await Bun.file("path/to/file.json").json();

// Write a file
await Bun.write("path/to/file.txt", "Hello, world!");
```
